  // Screen 23 - Play Online (the owner, 5 Oct 2026; the designer's online-match-options-prompts.md).
  // Rects are mockup pixels on 24-online-play-stake-100.png (1672 x 941). Its 50-coin twin,
  // 23-online-play-stake-50.png, is 1671 wide: stretched to 1672 it lines up with 24 within a pixel
  // (measured: offsets grow from 0 at the left edge to -1 px at the right), so 24 is the frame and 23
  // is compared after that stretch (check50/mockup-23-1672.png).
  //
  // Art (nothing is cut from the mockups):
  // - the shared menu background and UI kit: the back disc and icon, the wallet (the Earn Coins pill
  //   without its "+", coin and balance), the large panel, the crimson gold-rimmed play buttons with
  //   the light chevron, and the coin icon;
  // - the PlayOnline batch (ChatGPT-generated, ArtSource/Working/PlayOnline/notes.md; import settings in
  //   ArtSource/Kit/PlayOnline.json), at the rects its notes give: the subtitle's flourishes, the ivory
  //   badge (+ shadow) behind the lightning and behind the stacked coins (+ shadow), the dividers under
  //   the two mode titles and between the modes, the bright red Stake Match outline, the stake chips
  //   (one rect per chip for both looks, + shadow), the info button, and the prize popover (box, pointer
  //   and their shadows; the pointer is drawn over the box and its shadow under it, by
  //   PlayOnlineCustomizer), its brown x and its row lines.
  // Where a kit piece was fitted by the art batch (the wallet coin, the play buttons, the chip and row
  // coins), its rect is the fitted one; 100's coin sits halfway between where 24 and 23 draw it.
  //
  // Every word is a label. Fixed copy has a key; the presenter writes the rest: the balance, the chip
  // amounts (StakeRules.Stakes), "Play for {0} coins", "{0}-coin prizes" and the prizes
  // (StakeRules.PrizesFor). The texts below are 24's, as measured.
